=== 
--- calls
exit: 0
--- stdout
schwab-web — host wrapper

Subcommands:
  build                 Build the Docker image (`docker build`).
  download [args...]    One-shot CLI-MFA login + scrape. Pre-fills
                        from SCHWAB_LOGIN_ID / SCHWAB_PASSWORD,
                        auto-submits, prompts on stdin for the 2FA
                        code, runs the statements + tx-history
                        download, exits. Default range: 3 months
                        (widen with --lookback; --lookback all for a
                        full backfill, capped at Schwab's ~10 years).
                        Stdin must be a TTY.
  load [args...]        Parse bronze into the silver SQLite DB.
  collapse-statements [args...]
                        One-off reclaim of the statement-PDF bloat
                        Schwab creates by re-rendering each statement
                        on every download: collapse copies that parse
                        identically onto the oldest. Distinct from the
                        fleet `wealthdb-collect dedup` sweep (which only
                        hardlinks byte-identical files). Runs in-container
                        (needs the PDF parser). --dry-run prints the
                        evidence report (per-group plan + any divergent
                        groups) and collapses nothing.
  prune [args...]       Delete <run>/screenshots/ and stray
                        transactions/*/page-*.html from complete
                        dumps, whole non-complete dumps, and idle
                        entries of the /debug cache. Runs host-side
                        (pure stdlib Python; no Docker spawn), so it
                        reclaims disk even while a download container
                        is mid-flight. --dry-run prints the plan
                        without deleting.
  vnc-login [args...]   Fallback to a VNC-driven login + scrape
                        when the CLI-MFA selectors drift or a
                        non-code challenge is required. Starts
                        x11vnc on the first free 127.0.0.1 port in
                        5900-6000 (printed at start); tunnel and
                        connect a VNC client to it.
  sh|bash               Open an interactive shell in the container.
  help                  Show this message.

Mounted into the container:
  <TMP>/w-schwab-web/home/.secrets  ->  /secrets
  <TMP>/w-schwab-web/xdgdata/wealthdb/schwab-web     ->  /data
  <TMP>/w-schwab-web/xdgcache/wealthdb/startupcache  ->  /cache/startupcache
  <TMP>/w-schwab-web/xdgcache/wealthdb/schwab-web  ->  /cache/collector
  <TMP>/w-schwab-web/xdgcache/wealthdb/debug/schwab-web    ->  /debug
  <TMP>/w-schwab-web/tree/collectors/schwab-web  ->  /app

Override mounts via env:
  SCHWAB_WEB_SECRETS_DIR=/path/to/secrets
  SCHWAB_WEB_DATA_DIR=/path/to/data
  SCHWAB_WEB_DEBUG_DIR=/path/to/debug

Credentials:
  The Login ID is read from $SCHWAB_LOGIN_ID inside the container;
  the password from $SCHWAB_PASSWORD. When either is unset, the
  form is not pre-filled and Log In is driven by hand over
  vnc-login. The login script sources /secrets/schwab-web.env
  automatically (= $HOME/.secrets/schwab-web.env on the host).

  Use SINGLE QUOTES around values containing $, \!, backtick, or
  other shell metacharacters. Double quotes would let the host
  shell do $-expansion when sourcing the file, which silently
  mangles the password before it reaches the container:
    SCHWAB_LOGIN_ID='your-login-id'
    SCHWAB_PASSWORD='your-password-with-$pecial-chars'
  chmod 600 the file.
